    "note": "A held B keeps charging from 32 live ticks (the hum, with a rising tremolo, until the release) and is full at 44 (`charge_full`: the tick, exact to the event, one fixed sound so a release can be timed by ear). Live ticks are counted from the `tick` events that are not frozen, so a hit-stop does not move the hum. While a heavy winds up or charges it is armoured: a light never ends it and a medium only in its first 20 live ticks; a hit that does not end it gets the dull absorbed tick under it."
